            <div xml:id="d913">

                <pb facs="0951" n="831" sameAs="frus:frus1931v02/pg831"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.00 Bandit Activities, 1931/320:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in Honduras</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Higgins</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-12-02T15:00:00-05:00">December 2, 1931—3
                        p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>85. Your 182, December 1, 8 a.m., last paragraph. Department will be glad to have
                    Major Fassett visit the Danli region and feels that his visit may be
                    helpful.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
                <pb facs="0952" n="832" xml:id="pg832"/>
                <postscript>
                    <p>[On December 10 the Chargé in Nicaragua reported that General Matthews and
                        President Moncada had returned to Managua, and that the bandits were
                        believed to have “definitely withdrawn into their accustomed areas in
                        northern Nicaragua.” (817.00 Bandit Activities, 1931/339)]</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
